    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d107">

                <pb facs="0222" n="126" sameAs="frus:frus1900/pg126"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Conger to Mr. Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Pekin, China</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1900-05-18"><hi rendition="#italic">May 18,
                        1900</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 372.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to my dispatch No. 367<hi
                        rendition="#italic">a</hi> of the 3d instant, in which I reported the
                    departure of the U. S. S. <hi rendition="#italic">Wheeling</hi> for Shanghai, I
                    have the honor to inclose copy of my correspondence with Admiral Kempff, second
                    in command of United States naval force on Asiatic Station, confirming my
                    telegram requesting that a warship be sent to Taku as soon as possible.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">E. H. Conger.</hi></signed></closer>




                <xi:include href="d107-a1.xml" xpointer="d107-a1"/>
